        "original_id": "c9146c02-1fe2-5a83-ad8b-00ef0df75114",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tie Domi, Max Domi, Bill Watters, Paul Beeston, Bobby Orr\n- Organizations: Ontario Raiders, Maple Leaf Sports & Entertainment, Toronto Maple Leafs, Toronto Blue Jays, Toronto Rock\n- Places: Toronto, Maple Leaf Gardens\n- Roles: Assistant General Manager, president, player\n\nFacts:\n- Tahir \"Tie\" Domi was born on November 1, 1969, and he is a retired Canadian professional ice hockey player of Albanian origin.\n- Bill Watters was then the Assistant General Manager of the Toronto Maple Leafs, Paul Beeston was the former president of the Toronto Blue Jays, Tie Domi was a player for the Toronto Maple Leafs, and Bobby Orr was a former NHL player.\n- Maple Leaf Sports & Entertainment considered purchasing the Ontario Raiders, but a group including Bill Watters, Paul Beeston, Tie Domi, and Bobby Orr bought the team for $250,000 instead.\n- The purchasing group promptly relocated the Ontario Raiders to Toronto's Maple Leaf Gardens and rebranded the team as the Toronto Rock.\n- Max Domi's father is former Toronto Maple Leafs player Tie Domi.",
